# Ghost Watt configuration. Copy to .env.local and adjust.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. The app runs with an empty .env.local: every data
# provider below falls back to a built-in government table rather than to an
# error, and a scan with no vision model at all still returns a full costed
# audit from the room profile. Keys make the answers sharper, not possible.
#
# Never commit .env.local. Only this example file belongs in the repo.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Perception - how a photo gets read
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ghost Watt tries three things in order, and stops at the first that works:
#
#   1. Ollama on this machine     free, private, nothing uploaded
#   2. A hosted model             one key here, and no visitor needs their own
#   3. Room-profile estimate      always available, no model involved
#
# Local-only is the nicest mode and the default. But a DEPLOYED build probes for
# Ollama on the *server*, never finds it, and every visitor lands in mode 3 -
# so if anyone but you will use this, set one hosted key below.

# --- 1a. Local (no key, no account, no cloud) ---

# Where the local Ollama daemon is listening.
OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Which local vision model to use for perception.
# 8GB RAM:  moondream        (~1.7GB, fast, CPU-friendly)   <- default
# 12GB+:    qwen2.5vl:3b     (sharper device/state reading)
# 16GB+:    llama3.2-vision  (most capable)
OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL=moondream

# Max time to wait for one image (ms). CPU inference can be slow.
OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# --- 1b. Hosted fallback: set exactly ONE of these ---
# Whichever is set wins, in the order listed. Each also takes an optional
# <NAME>_MODEL override, e.g. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5.

# Recommended. Best device recognition of the four; Haiku-size is cheap.
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Has a genuinely free tier, and is by far the fastest to answer.
# https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# One key, many models. https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Force a specific engine instead of letting the chain decide.
# One of: ollama | anthropic | groq | openai | openrouter
VISION_PROVIDER=

# Max time to wait on a hosted vision call (ms).
VISION_TIMEOUT_MS=45000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Data providers - free, server-side only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys are read on the server and never sent to the browser. /settings shows
# which are configured as booleans and never displays a value.

# EIA open data - THE ONE WORTH HAVING. A single key buys two features:
#   - the real commercial price for this state this month, instead of a stored
#     average that slowly goes stale
#   - the hourly grid fuel mix (EIA-930), which Ghost Watt turns into a live
#     carbon intensity: the same projector left on overnight costs roughly twice
#     the carbon at 3am on a still night as it does at 1pm under full sun
# Free at: https://www.eia.gov/opendata/register.php   (instant, email only)
# Without: the built-in 51-state table in src/lib/grid.ts.
EIA_API_KEY=

# OpenWeather - current conditions and degree days at the building.
# Buys:    HVAC and space-heater findings get read against outdoor temperature,
#          so the report can flag a heater running in July as a fault, not a habit.
#          Needs coordinates on the building (Settings -> location).
# Free at: https://openweathermap.org/api              (free tier, 60 calls/min)
# Note:    a brand-new key returns 401 for up to a couple of hours after signup.
#          That is activation lag, not a bad key - wait rather than regenerating.
# Without: HVAC findings are reported without weather context.
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=

# NREL utility rates - resolves a lat/lon to the utility that actually serves it.
# Buys:    a school on a municipal utility gets its own rate rather than the
#          state average, which can be off by a factor of two either way.
# Free at: https://api.data.gov/signup/                (instant)
#          One api.data.gov key works across all NREL APIs.
# Note:    leaving this blank is fine - the app falls back to the shared
#          DEMO_KEY, which needs no signup and is rate-limited to a few calls
#          an hour. Good enough to try, not good enough to deploy on.
# Without: the state average.
NREL_API_KEY=

# Electricity Maps - OPTIONAL OVERRIDE, no longer needed.
# Their free tier is gone. Carbon intensity now comes from EIA-930 using the
# EIA_API_KEY above, which is free and returns the whole 24-hour shape rather
# than a single current value. Set this only if you already hold a paid key.
ELECTRICITY_MAPS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Class mode - the shared session store
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Upstash Redis (REST) - what makes a whole-class audit work on a real deployment.
# Buys:    thirty phones scanning thirty corridors into one live building map.
# Free at: https://console.upstash.com/                (no card, instant)
#          Create a database, then copy the REST URL and REST token.
# Note:    a Vercel KV database is Upstash underneath, so if you deploy on Vercel
#          the KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN it injects are picked up
#          automatically and you can leave both of these blank.
# Without: sessions live in the server's memory. Fine on a laptop and fine for a
#          demo, but on a deployment that runs more than one instance two phones
#          can land on two instances and never see each other. The /class page
#          says so on screen rather than failing quietly.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
